{"id":"en-106","title":"Connect XT&XRF Model To LightBurn Via USB Cable","family":"x-series","topic":"guides","read_minutes":1,"source_url":"https://wiki.1laser.com/en/x-series/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable","source_updated_at":"2025-12-18T08:13:20.651Z","body_html":"<div><h2 id=\"connect-xtxrf-model-to-lightburn-via-usb-cable\"> Connect XT&amp;XRF Model To LightBurn Via USB Cable</h2>\n<p>Learn how to connect your OneLaser XT or XRF to LightBurn via USB. Follow this simple setup guide to install LightBurn, configure Ruida, set origin, and start engraving.</p><div>\n\n</div><figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable.jpg\" alt=\"USB connection setup for OneLaser XT and XRF machines\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><h2 id=\"operational-guide\"> Operational Guide</h2><div>\n\n</div><p>1. Install the LightBurn software, please see the link below to install:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://docs.lightburnsoftware.com/latest/GetStarted/InstallLightBurn/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Install the LightBurn software</a></p><div>\n\n</div><p>2. Connect your computer and laser machine with a USB cable.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_2.jpg\" alt=\"Plugging USB cable into OneLaser machine\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>3. Open LightBurn and set a connection.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_3.jpg\" alt=\"Opening LightBurn software to create device connection\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>4. Select Ruida.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_4.jpg\" alt=\"Selecting Ruida controller in LightBurn\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>5. Select Serial/USB.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_5.jpg\" alt=\"Choosing Serial USB connection option in LightBurn\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>6. Name your laser and enter the work area — for X Series, the area is 600 × 300 mm.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_6.jpg\" alt=\"Entering device name and work area size for OneLaser X Series\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>7. Set the Rear Left as Origin.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_7.jpg\" alt=\"Setting rear left origin position in LightBurn\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>8. Then it&#x27;s finish.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_8.jpg\" alt=\"LightBurn device setup completion screen\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div><p>9. Back to the home page and select XT. If it shows “Ready,” it means the software is connected.</p>\n<figure>\n  <img src=\"https://wiki.1laser.com/x-series/set-up/connect-via-usb-cable/connect-lightburn-via-usb-cable_9.jpg\" alt=\"LightBurn showing OneLaser XT device ready status\" loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\">\n</figure><div>\n\n</div></div>","headings":[{"level":1,"id":"connect-xtxrf-model-to-lightburn-via-usb-cable","text":"Connect XT&XRF Model To LightBurn Via USB Cable"},{"level":2,"id":"operational-guide","text":"Operational Guide"}],"technical_version":"unknown"}